---
title: "completeTempRegistration (AttendanceZen: Blueprint)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_validate_token: SELECT * FROM attendance.temp_registrations WHERE token = token
    q_validate_token --> q_invalid_token: tempReg not found
    q_invalid_token --> [*]: return success=false, "invalid token"
    q_validate_token --> q_check_completed: tempReg found
    q_check_completed --> q_already_completed: tempReg.completed_at is set
    q_already_completed --> [*]: return success=false, "already completed"
    q_check_completed --> q_normalize_card: completed_at is null
    q_normalize_card --> q_check_duplicate: normalizedCardId = cardId.toLowerCase().replace(/:/, '')
    q_check_duplicate --> q_card_exists: SELECT attendance.users WHERE card_id = normalizedCardId finds record
    q_card_exists --> [*]: return success=false, "card already in use"
    q_check_duplicate --> q_insert_user: no existing user with this card
    q_insert_user --> q_insert_error: INSERT INTO attendance.users fails
    q_insert_error --> [*]: return success=false, "user registration failed"
    q_insert_user --> q_mark_complete: INSERT succeeds with user_id from tempReg
    q_mark_complete --> q_success: UPDATE temp_registrations SET completed_at = now WHERE token = token
    q_success --> [*]: return success=true, "registration complete"

    note right of q_validate_token
        INV-001: token must exist and not be already completed
        INV-002: card_id must be unique across attendance.users
        INV-003: user_id is linked from temp_registrations to attendance.users
    end note
